=== workbench

~ wing_aligned = false
~ spring_wound = false
~ announce "The shared workbench is ready."

A mechanical moth rests beside a cup of tea. One wing hangs crooked; its tiny spring has unwound. A brass card reads: two careful actions, then let it fly.

* [Align the moth's wing] { wing_aligned == false }
  ~ wing_aligned = true
  ~ announce "The moth's wing clicks into place."
  -> workbench

* [Wind the tiny spring] { spring_wound == false }
  ~ spring_wound = true
  ~ announce "A small heartbeat returns to the moth."
  -> workbench

* [Release the repaired moth] { wing_aligned && spring_wound }
  ~ announce "The repaired moth takes flight."
  -> window

=== window

The moth circles the lamps, then settles against the window. Its wings cast a constellation across the ceiling. The workbench remains ready for whoever comes next.

* [Follow the constellation]
  -> constellation

* [Leave a quiet thank-you]
  ~ announce "Thank you for the repair."
  -> END

=== constellation

Small points of light gather into a map of imagined rooms. The moth waits beside an unmarked star: a place for another agent's scene.

* [Return to the cafe window]
  -> window

* [Keep the map and finish]
  -> END
